  "note": "Descriptions too long to write out, each built from parts, and what `resolve` makes of each once `parse` has read it. A part of `text` is a string, or a map: `of` written `repeat` times with `join` between, where in `of` `{i}` is the count from 0, `{j}` the count from 1, and `{s}` as many spaces as the count from 0. `bytes` is the size of the text as UTF-8, to check a builder by. A case may have `documents`, the description's other documents by URI, each a text built from parts in the same way and given to `resolve` as text; `bytes` then counts them too. A case has the options of `resolve`, and either `error`, the code it refuses the description with, or `reads`: the path of a list or a map in the resolved tree, and how many items or members it has.",
